From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:16:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] irqchip: qcom-mpm: do not require MPM coverage for
 clock event timers

The broadcast arch_mem_timer (GIC SPI 39, IRQF_TIMER) is shut down by
tick and timekeeping suspend before MSM8226 system sleep, which wakes on
device and RTC interrupts only. It was the one interrupt that made
qcom_mpm_sleep_ready() refuse deep suspend.

Assisted-by: LLM [Claude Code]
---
 drivers/irqchip/irq-qcom-mpm.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/irqchip/irq-qcom-mpm.c b/drivers/irqchip/irq-qcom-mpm.c
index 623bc755b..37b02e5f2 100644
--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-qcom-mpm.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-qcom-mpm.c
@@ -494,7 +494,13 @@ static bool qcom_mpm_wake_covered(struct qcom_mpm_priv *priv)
 			if (data->domain == priv->domain->parent && data->hwirq < 32)
 				continue;
 			for (action = desc->action; action; action = action->next)
-				if (action->flags & IRQF_NO_SUSPEND)
+				/*
+				 * Clock event timers (IRQF_TIMER implies NO_SUSPEND) are shut
+				 * down by tick/timekeeping suspend; system RAM sleep wakes on
+				 * device and RTC interrupts, not on a Linux tick.
+				 */
+				if ((action->flags & IRQF_NO_SUSPEND) &&
+				    !(action->flags & __IRQF_TIMER))
 					required = true;
 		}
 		if (required && !qcom_mpm_irq_covered(priv, data)) {
